Z||000000||DISenchanted||11-08-1999||02:55 PM||||Ok, I've put this off for long enough and now it's raining down here in Southern California.  My sun roof is leaking.  I need to know where I can aquire the parts.<BR>I need the bolts that attach to the glass, all of them.  I need the little metal prongs for the front, and anything else that might be helpful.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88 Fiero||11-08-1999||03:26 PM||||Try and email TOM...he local to us and might have the parts that he needed...Anyway, did you ever got resolve on all of your car problems???||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||11-08-1999||05:23 PM||||Can anyone provide a source for the rubber gasket around the sunroof opening?  Is this common to all Pontiac sunroofs?  Mine is degrading.||||reg||5
Z||000003||Carrolles||11-08-1999||05:37 PM||||All the parts are still available from the Pontiac dealership.<BR>Galaxy Automotive ((800) 225-1113) offers 20% discount to Fiero Club members.  Just tell them you are with the Fiero club (it doesn't matter which one, they don't ask).||||reg||1
Z||000004||88 Fiero||11-08-1999||05:42 PM||||I think the Fiero Store sells it too...I don't know how much..probably around $35.00 to $75.00 for that gasket...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||11-08-1999||06:33 PM||||<BR>This may or may not be of any interest, but I shimmed the latch at the back that holds the sunroof down. It now pulls my sunroof down real snug.<P>Here in Vancouver it's very important to have a car that doesn't leak in the rain. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000006||Cooter||11-08-1999||08:40 PM||||Before you replace the sunroof gasket, fix the seals around the glass mounting hardware. I just went to the hardware store and bought some flat black rubber washers to go on both sides of the glass. I then filled the hole in the glass around the bolt with some clear silicone to make sure nothing got by the washers. I just wish that I had done this before I replaced the sunroof gasket because the gasket was not the source of the leaks, but the cracked rubber around the hardware.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Wolfhound||11-08-1999||08:57 PM||||Exactly Cooter, also remove the glass and clean the gasket. Also check that he lockdown mechinism is not loose.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||11-08-1999||09:24 PM||||Fiero Store price = $65.75||||reg||1
Z||000009||TOM||11-08-1999||10:16 PM||||I have noticed that the early years dont have the drain holes in the roof. I drilled them out and now it is fine. They let the water drain off before it gets high enough to leak in||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carrolles||11-08-1999||10:32 PM||||After I had ordered the sunroof gasket to fix my leaky roof Ed Parks suggested that I replace the bolts/seals for the hinges and latch mechanism.  He said in 99.9% of the leaky roofs he sees this is the fix.  It was for mine.  I found a buyer for my gasket.<BR>The new hinge plates have the plastic coating that was missing on mine.  This tightened up the top considerably.  Also I agree that you should clean the gasket thoroughly and treat it with silicone spray.<P>I think the total cost for the seals/bolts and hinge plates was less than $20.00 and I got everything from the Pontiac dealer.||||reg||1
